===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|originally|_|slang|usually|_|pejorative}} An [[obese]] or otherwise swollen [[ankle]] that blends into the [[calf]] without clear demarcation.
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2001|title=w:Shallow Hal|writers=w:Peter Farrelly; w:Bobby Farrelly|passage=Hey, all l’m saying is she’s got '''cankles''', for God’s sake. ''What?'' '''Cankles'''! She’s got no ankles. It’s like the calf merged with the foot, cut out the middleman.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|passage=The “'''cankle'''” (or the appearance of not having an ankle, but the calf of the leg just connecting to the foot) is a look that many women have and most could live without.|author=Jeff Smith|title=Posing for Portrait Photography: A Head-to-Toe Guide}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|passage=They’d pass me magazines and ask how my '''cankle''' recovery was progressing. They’re ankles, not '''cankles'''. I don’t have '''cankles'''!|author=Franz Wisner|title=Honeymoon with my Brother}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2007|title=Family Guy|season=5|number=13|episode=w:Bill & Peter's Bogus Journey|passage=Now that's a '''cankle'''! Where does the calf fat end and the ankle fat begin? Who knows, that's the fun!}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=13 September 2008|title=Saturday Night Live|actor=w:Amy Poehler|role=Hillary Clinton|passage=Stop saying I have '''cankles'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2017-01-27|author=Pierre Andre; Eckart Haneke; Leonardo Marini; Christopher Rowland Payne|title=Cosmetic Medicine and Surgery|publisher=CRC Press|isbn=9781482256802
|text=Laserassisted lipolysis for '''cankle''' remodelling: A prospective study in 30 patients. Lasers Med Sci 2014; 29:131–136. Leclère FM, Trelles M, MorenoMoraga J, Servell P, Unglaub F, Mordon SR. 980nm laser lipolysis (LAL): About 674{{nb...}}}}

====Usage notes====
Although originally and colloquially used with negative connotations, the term is increasingly used in neutral and medical-scientific contexts. It is even occasionally used affectionately. This condition is often seen in Uptown area of New Orleans.

